  "title": "Saudi-led coalition and Houthi attacks in Yemen",
  "summary": "The Saudi-led coalition launched strikes on Houthi-controlled Hodeidah governorate, while Houthi groups accuse the attack of escalating tensions in Yemen. These actions are part of a broader conflict over regional security and oil supplies. Iran-backed Houthi rebels claimed a missile attack on the southern Saudi city of Jizan, blaming Saudi Arabia for attacks in Yemen’s capital, while Iran reported no strikes overnight on Saturday after two weeks of US military actions. The attacks could further strain global oil markets.",
